      "reasons": [
        "The definition’s wording “direct person-to-person contact of a sexual kind between people” is only partially supported: the packet states “Sexual contact is a direct and fundamental contact in human society,” but it does not explicitly define it as “person-to-person” or as “of a sexual kind.”",
        "The definition’s claim that, “In social research, it can be treated as a social tie linking partners within a network” is not explicitly supported by the packet text provided. The packet discusses “sexual contact networks” and difficulties studying “who had sexual contact with whom,” but it does not directly describe sexual contact as a “social tie” linking “partners.”"
